		"notes": "\n\t<p><i>Like a hunter's lure, a small woodland animal is perched atop a tree trunk. In reality, the tree conceals toothy jaws that devour reckless hunters.</i></p>\n\t<p></p>\n\t<p><strong>AC</strong> 10, <strong>HP</strong> 28, <strong>ATK</strong> 2 bite +5 (1d8), <strong>MV</strong> close (burrow, climb), <strong>S</strong> +2, <strong>D</strong> -1, <strong>C</strong> +1, <strong>I</strong> -2, <strong>W</strong> +0, <strong>Ch</strong> -3, <strong>AL</strong> N, <strong>LV</strong> 6</p><p></p>\n\t<p><strong>Implant</strong>. Lay eggs inside a mortal, eating its lure. CON 15+ or 1d4 CON damage (cannot heal while ill). Repeat check once per day; ends on success. Die at 0 CON, spawning a juvenile wolf-in- sheep's-clothing which bursts from the corpse and devours it.</p><p></p>\n\t<p><i>Shadowfinder Complete Bestiary</i></p>",
